---
import SiteLayout from '../components/SiteLayout.astro';
import ProductPreview from '../components/ProductPreview.astro';
import TechnicalFlow from '../components/TechnicalFlow.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
const title = 'Ember — Monero mining, without the mystery';
const description = 'A clearer way to run and understand Monero mining on Windows, with practical guides and transparent product information.';
---
<SiteLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="home-hero" aria-labelledby="home-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <div class="eyebrow">A calmer way to mine</div>
        <h1 id="home-title">Monero mining,<br /><em>without the</em><br />mystery.</h1>
        <p>Ember is Windows software for setting up and understanding Monero CPU mining, with the choices and session state kept clear.</p>
        <div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/ember/">Explore Ember <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
        <div class="fine-print">IN DEVELOPMENT <span aria-hidden="true">/</span> NO PUBLIC RELEASE YET</div>
      </div>
      <ProductPreview />
    </section>
    <section class="section split-section" aria-labelledby="principles-title">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">A better kind of clarity</div><h2 id="principles-title" class="manifesto">Mining should make sense before it's <em>running.</em></h2></div>
      <ul class="principle-grid"><li><span class="principle-icon"><Icon name="magnifyingGlass" size="section" /></span><strong>VISIBLE</strong><p>Setup choices and observed mining state stay in view.</p></li><li><span class="principle-icon"><Icon name="playCircle" size="section" /></span><strong>CONTROLLED</strong><p>Review does not start mining; starting is a separate action.</p></li><li><span class="principle-icon"><Icon name="cpu" size="section" /></span><strong>LOCAL</strong><p>The Windows app supervises its own XMRig process on the machine.</p></li><li><span class="principle-icon"><Icon name="info" size="section" /></span><strong>TRANSPARENT</strong><p>Observed, unavailable and still-in-development states remain distinct.</p></li></ul>
    </section>
    <section class="section" id="how-it-works" aria-label="How Monero mining fits together"><TechnicalFlow /></section>
    <section class="section" aria-labelledby="knowledge-title">
      <div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow">A useful place to start</div><h2 id="knowledge-title">Good answers for the work in front of you.</h2><p>A small, carefully built reference for learning the concepts, making setup choices and diagnosing issues without guesswork.</p></div>
      <div class="discovery-grid"><a class="discovery-card" href="/learn/"><span class="discovery-index">01 / UNDERSTAND</span><h3>Learn</h3><p>Clear explanations of Monero mining, RandomX, hashrate and pools.</p><span class="text-link">Explore concepts <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a><a class="discovery-card" href="/guides/"><span class="discovery-index">02 / DO</span><h3>Guides</h3><p>Practical walkthroughs that explain the choices behind each step.</p><span class="text-link">Browse guide paths <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a><a class="discovery-card" href="/troubleshoot/"><span class="discovery-index">03 / DIAGNOSE</span><h3>Troubleshoot</h3><p>Make sense of XMRig and Windows issues, with safe next steps.</p><span class="text-link">Find an issue <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a></div>
    </section>
    <section class="section" aria-label="Ember trust and transparency"><div class="trust-band"><span class="trust-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⌁</span><div><h3>Trust is part of the product.</h3><p>See how Ember handles setup, wallet information, XMRig and the work still ahead of public release.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/trust/">Read the trust notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    <section class="section"><div class="cta-panel"><div class="eyebrow">EMBER / WINDOWS DESKTOP</div><h2>A more understandable way to approach Monero mining.</h2><p>Ember is being developed in the open. Public release is not ready while production mining verification and release checks remain in progress.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="/ember/">About Ember <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href="/trust/">Current development status</a></div></div></section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
